<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tongeren</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Atuatuca Tungrorum, Tongres</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tongeren is a town in the province of Limburg in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and claims to be the oldest town in the country. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atuatuca">Atuatuca</a> Tungrorum it was founded under Augustus as the chief town of the Tungri and grew into a walled Roman city on the road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavay">Bavay</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>. In the 4th century it was the see of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/servatius">Servatius</a>, from which the bishopric later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maastricht">Maastricht</a> and then Liège.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tongeren.jpg" alt="Tongeren" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: original: Jeanhousen; derivative work by P199 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20100706_tongeren25-c.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
